---
// "Why trailhead" band: three value-proposition cards.
---

<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">Why trailhead</span>
    <h2 class="h2">A shared map, an engine that builds</h2>
    <p class="sub">Give a big, foggy idea a place to begin and a disciplined way to walk it to a working result, with the whole plan living on your issue tracker instead of scattered local files.</p>
    <div class="props">
      <div class="prop">
        <div class="ic"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M9 20l-5.4 1.8 1.8-5.4L16 5l4 4L9 20z"/><path d="M12 8l4 4"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Everything on GitHub Issues</h3>
        <p>The map is a parent issue, each ticket a child, discussion and plans are comments. No <code>.planning/</code> directory: the repo holds code, the plan stays visible to the whole team.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="prop">
        <div class="ic"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 2v4M12 18v4M2 12h4M18 12h4"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Execution inside the map</h3>
        <p>Not plan-and-hand-off. Build tickets graduate from the fog and are executed as children of the map, discuss &rarr; plan &rarr; execute &rarr; verify, with atomic commits.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="prop">
        <div class="ic"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M17 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H5a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"/><path d="M23 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Built for teams</h3>
        <p>The tracker is the single source of truth. Claim a ticket to lock it, work a shared frontier one ticket per session, isolate concurrent work, pause, resume, split.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
